        "bigcap": {
          "top": 580,
          "text": "Articles *hours before* the announcement|And now, a *police investigation*",
          "size": 60,
          "cue": "hours"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b03",
      "accent": [
        "5:15",
        "several hours"
      ],
      "text": "Voting had closed in late September. On October 26, shortly after 5:15 in the afternoon, London time, articles started circulating. The ceremony, at the London Palladium, was still several hours away.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "clip",
        "shots": [
          "afp_a",
          "cgtn_b"
        ],
        "tag": {
          "right": 120,
          "top": 90,
          "value": "5:15 PM",
          "label": "London, 26 Oct",
          "cue": "5:15"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b04",
      "accent": [
        "three",
        "Yamal"
      ],
      "text": "And the site did not name one winner. It published articles for several. Harry Kane. Kylian Mbappé. Lamine Yamal. One of them said Mbappé wins the Ballon d'Or thanks to his consistency at the highest levels.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "trio",
        "cues": [
          "Kane",
          "Kylian",
          "Lamine"
        ],
        "items": [
          {
            "kicker": "AN ARTICLE ON",
            "img": "kane3",
            "value": "KANE"
          },
          {
            "kicker": "AN ARTICLE ON",
            "img": "mbappe1",
            "value": "MBAPPÉ"
          },
          {
            "kicker": "AN ARTICLE ON",
            "img": "yamal1",
            "value": "YAMAL"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b05",
      "accent": [
        "in advance",
        "unclear"
      ],
      "text": "One possible explanation, according to the reports, is that the organisers had prepared several articles in advance, ready to publish once the winner was announced. But the same reports say it is unclear how they went live.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "clip",
        "shots": [
          "sky_win"
        ],
        "bigcap": {
          "top": 590,
          "text": "“One possible explanation is that the organizers had prepared several articles in advance.”",
          "size": 50,
          "src": "As reported by beIN SPORTS, October 26",
          "cue": "possible"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b06",
      "accent": [
        "12",
        "France Football"
      ],
      "text": "Then came the second part. On November 9 it was reported that France Football, the magazine that runs the Ballon d'Or, had filed a complaint. Investigators suspect that the owners of 12 accounts on a predictions platform had got hold of information that was not yet public.",
      "visual": {
        "type": "clip",
        "shots": [
          "cgtn_c"
        ],
        "tag": {
          "right": 120,
          "top": 90,
          "value": "12",
          "label": "accounts, predictions platform",
          "cue": "12"
        },
        "bigcap": {
          "top": 620,
          "text": "France Football *filed a complaint*",
          "cue": "filed"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b07",
      "accent": [
        "200,000",
        "unproven"
      ],
      "text": "Those accounts are reported to have made profits of nearly 200,000 euros net. That is a suspicion. It has not been proven, and the report I read names no juror and no player.",
      "visual": {
